  "body": "An ordinary caller can reuse the first post-write field observation as the second writer's input in both field orders, 1→0 and 0→1. This selected explicit-unit-return path checks separate originals of the same nominal, each authentic field, the Copy carried to the second actual, both displaced values and full loan cleanup. Generated C17 reads the first target once in the selected shape.\n\nThe integrated build reproduces #1801's ordinary unit completion and the existing equal-position snapshots byte for byte. Mixed displaced-byte handoffs and ordinary-completion snapshots refuse, including both mixed positions and both normal ending forms. The sibling, stale, wrong-original and escape checks preserve output custody. [#1801](https://github.com/wakairo/NewLang_Compiler/pull/1801) · [Integrated LOCAL READY](https://github.com/wakairo/NewLang_Compiler/issues/1802#issuecomment-7163580247)\n\n- The original Gate0 recorded CHECK success and C17 refusal for both mixed-position snapshots. The new integrated outputs match the first private implementation byte for byte. The original FIRST, raw results and candidate have been preserved. [FIRST](https://github.com/wakairo/NewLang_Compiler/issues/1802#issuecomment-7162603814) · [Original LOCAL READY](https://github.com/wakairo/NewLang_Compiler/issues/1802#issuecomment-7162847890) · [Original evidence](https://github.com/wakairo/NewLang_Evidence/tree/626854602b5b22b5b290dadf14c668fc45e7a2c3/p1802/gate0)\n- Both GCC Release and Clang ASan/LSan+UBSan passed 29 CLI rows and 12 selected CTests. Native passed 130/130. Rollback #247 covers 1,632 CHECK, 16 entry-seal and 2,479 named C17 cases per output state with an effective 180 s timeout.\n- HEAD `0610baef571243ee5dc326b2a7a908c0b66c2263`, tree `2401aaef1c39d32af7a95b81cd78a72e46832033`, sole parent `1c99d8dfc536160dfd1b26016cd4414dc1af9b75`. The full-index diff spans 6 paths and 6,513 bytes with SHA-256 `8bb353f096431b929c08d319329899353a0815ac3f7106c0518832a78b51e894`. [DRAFT GO](https://github.com/wakairo/NewLang_Compiler/issues/1802#issuecomment-7163603079)\n\nRefs #1802.",
